The `logCondition` function takes four arguments: `condition`, `severity`, `format`, and `...`. It first checks for NULL arguments and errors opening the log file using `openLogFile`. If there are no errors, it formats the message using `vsnprintf` and writes it to the log file using `writeLogEntry`. Finally, it closes the log file and cleans up resources using `closeLogFile`.

