The `semaphore` variable is used to acquire and release slots for concurrent asynchronous operations. The `throttleRate` constant defines the rate at which external API calls are made, while the `cacheDuration` constant sets the duration for which results of external API calls are cached.

The `customAccumulator` function is used to handle more complex types beyond simple numbers, such as arrays and objects. The `reportProgress` function provides a callback for reporting progress of the reduction process.

The function returns the final reduced value or an error if one occurs, while adhering to all the given constraints and scenarios.

