The `BatchProcessingSystem` class includes three main functionalities: data validation, transformation, and error handling and recovery. The system utilizes parallel processing techniques, such as thread pools and task queues, to handle multiple files simultaneously and efficiently. It also optimizes performance by ensuring that it can handle files up to 10GB in size.

The system is designed to be fault-tolerant and scalable, capable of supporting hundreds of thousands of files being processed daily with low-latency response times even under high load. It includes features for job scheduling, retry mechanisms, and notifications for job completion or failure. The system also provides real-time monitoring and logging capabilities, allowing administrators to track the progress and health of the processing jobs.

