```c
#include <openssl/evp.h>
#include <openssl/md5.h>
#include <openssl/sha.h>
#include <openssl/camellia.h>

int initCryptPrimitives(void) {
    // Add AES and Camellia block ciphers to OpenSSL library
    if (EVP_add_cipher(EVP_get_cipherbyname("aes-128-cbc")) == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (EVP_add_cipher(EVP_get_cipherbyname("camellia-128-cbc")) == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }

    // Add MD5 and SHA digests to OpenSSL library
    if (EVP_add_digest(EVP_get_digestbyname("md5")) == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (EVP_add_digest(EVP_get_digestbyname("sha1")) == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }

    // Add any necessary aliases for cryptographic primitives
    EVP_add_alias("aes-256-cbc", "camellia-256-cbc");
    EVP_add_alias("md5", "sha1");

    return 1;
}
```
This function uses the OpenSSL library to add essential cryptographic primitives, including AES and Camellia block ciphers, MD5, SHA, and SHA1 digests. It also adds any necessary aliases for these primitives. The function returns a non-zero value if any of the additions fail, indicating that some cryptographic primitive could not be added to the OpenSSL library. If all additions are successful, the function returns 1.

To handle errors and gracefully degrade in case external services like the payment gateway or email verification service are unavailable, you can use error handling mechanisms such as checking the return values of the `EVP_add_cipher` and `EVP_add_digest` functions for NULL, and returning an appropriate status code. For example:
