    return 0;
}
```
In this example, if either of the `aes-128-cbc` or `md5` cryptographic primitives cannot be added to the OpenSSL library, the function returns a non-zero value indicating an error. You can also use more robust error handling mechanisms such as logging and reporting the errors to a centralized log management system.

