The class is designed to be thread-safe and capable of handling large-scale deployments efficiently by limiting the number of concurrent DNS queries to prevent resource exhaustion and performance degradation. The timeout mechanism ensures that the function does not wait indefinitely during DNS resolution.

Note that this code requires a mocking library called `blueslip` for isolation between tests, which must be reset after each test using the `reset()` function to maintain performance and ease of future updates.

