            @Override
            public MediaType contentType() {
                return MediaType.parse("application/octet-stream");
            }

            @Override
            public long contentLength() throws IOException {
                return inputStream.available();
            }

            @Override
            public void writeTo(BufferedSink sink) throws IOException {
                sink.writeAll(Okio.source(inputStream));
            }
        };
        Request request = new Request.Builder()
                .url(BASE_URL + "/" + bucketName + "/" + objectKey)
                .put(body)
                .build();
        httpClient.newCall(request).execute();
    }

    public void deleteObject(String bucketName, String objectKey) throws IOException {
        Request request = new Request.Builder()
                .url(BASE_URL + "/" + bucketName + "/" + objectKey)
                .delete()
                .build();
        httpClient.newCall(request).execute();
    }

    public List<String> getObjects(String bucketName) throws IOException {
        Request request = new Request.Builder()
                .url(BASE_URL + "/" + bucketName)
                .get()
                .build();
        Response response = httpClient.newCall(request).execute();
        List<String> objects = new ArrayList<>();
        for (JsonNode node : mapper.readTree(response.body().string())) {
            String objectKey = node.get("key").asText();
            objects.add(objectKey);
        }
        return objects;
    }
}
```
This code defines a `S3Client` class that provides methods for interacting with an S3 bucket. The `S3Client` constructor takes in the name of the bucket and the AWS credentials to use for authentication. The `getObject`, `putObject`, and `deleteObject` methods are used for getting, putting, and deleting objects from the bucket respectively. The `getObjects` method is used for listing all the objects in a bucket.

