public MoSTState fetchAndProcessState(String filePath) throws DFSClientNotAvailableException, NetworkConnectivityException, ClassLoadingException {
    // Use a temporary directory to store the downloaded state object
    File tempDir = Files.createTempDirectory("MoSTState").toFile();

    // Download the state object from the remote file path using the DFS client library
    try {
        dfsClient.download(filePath, tempDir.getAbsolutePath());
    } catch (DFSClientNotAvailableException e) {
        throw new DFSClientNotAvailableException("Unable to connect to the DFS client", e);
    } catch (NetworkConnectivityException e) {
        throw new NetworkConnectivityException("Network connection error while fetching state object", e);
    }

    // Load the state object from the downloaded file using ObjectInputStream
    File stateFile = new File(tempDir, "state.obj");
    ObjectInputStream ois = null;
    try {
        ois = new ObjectInputStream(new GZIPInputStream(new BufferedInputStream(Files.newInputStream(Paths.get(stateFile.toURI())))));
        MoSTState state = (MoSTState) ois.readObject();
        return state;
    } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
        throw new ClassLoadingException("Unable to load state object", e);
    } finally {
        if (ois != null) {
            try {
                ois.close();
            } catch (IOException e) {
                // ignore
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This implementation uses a temporary directory to store the downloaded state object and then loads it using an `ObjectInputStream` instance created from a `GZIPInputStream` wrapping a `BufferedInputStream` around the input stream of the state file. The method also catches and handles the following exceptions:

* `DFSClientNotAvailableException`: thrown when the DFS client library is not available or cannot be connected to.
* `NetworkConnectivityException`: thrown when there is a network connection error while fetching the state object.
* `ClassLoadingException`: thrown when an exception occurs during loading of the state object (e.g., when the class of the state object is not found).

