The code first checks if the input directory contains any image files using the `ListImageFiles` function, which lists all the files in the input directory and subdirectories that match the pattern "*.jpg", "*.png" or "*.gif". If no image files are found, it prints an error message to the console.

After that, the code creates a new PDF document from the list of images using the `CreatePdfDocument` function. The `CreatePdfDocument` function takes two arguments: the list of image files and the name of the output PDF file. It uses the `magick convert` command to create the new PDF file from the image files.

The code then frees the memory allocated for the PDF document and the list of images.

