      System.err.println("Error writing compressed BMP image to file: " + e.getMessage());
    } finally {
      if (outputStream != null) {
        try {
          outputStream.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
          // ignore
        }
      }
    }
  }

  /**
   * Convert OpenCV Mat object to BufferedImage for compression.
   */
  public static BufferedImage matToBufferedImage(Mat inputMat) {
    int type = BufferedImage.TYPE_BYTE_GRAY;
    if (inputMat.channels() > 1) {
      type = BufferedImage.TYPE_3BYTE_BGR;
    }
    BufferedImage image = new BufferedImage(inputMat.cols(), inputMat.rows(), type);
    WritableRaster raster = image.getRaster();
    DataBuffer buffer = raster.getDataBuffer();
    byte[] data = buffer.getData();
    inputMat.get(0, 0, data);
    return image;
  }
}
```

This code uses the OpenCV library to perform the image processing tasks and the Java ImageIO API for writing the compressed images to disk. The `compressImage` method takes in an OpenCV Mat object as input and returns a Map<String, Object> that contains the compression settings used during the compression process. The `compressJpegImage`, `compressPngImage`, and `compressBmpImage` methods perform the actual image compression tasks using the Java ImageIO API and return a File object representing the output file. The `matToBufferedImage` method converts an OpenCV Mat object to a BufferedImage object that can be used for compression.

