The `dynamicTrimAndCapitalize` function is used to trim and capitalize the specified words from the beginning and end of an input string. This function uses the `strtok` and `strncmp` functions to tokenize the input string and compare each word with the list of trim words. The `strncat` function is used to concatenate the trimmed words in the resulting string, while the `strlen` function is used to calculate the total length of the resulting string.

