The `analyzeText` method takes a string of text as input and returns an object with the number of occurrences of each book in the text. The method also allows for integration with an external API using the `verifyExistenceInDatabase` method, which verifies the presence of the extracted books in databases of religious texts.

The `runTests` function takes no arguments and runs a series of tests to ensure the correctness of the code. The function uses a mocking library called `blueslip` to isolate each test from the others and maintain proper cleanup even in the presence of errors. The function also logs information to the console for each test, allowing users to track the frequency of each book's occurrence in the analyzed texts.

