<?php
class SecurePasswordManager {
    public static function generateRandomString($length) {
        $characters = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789!@#$%^&*()-_=+';
        $randomString = '';
        for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
            $index = rand(0, strlen($characters) - 1);
            $randomString .= $characters[$index];
        }
        return $randomString;
    }
}
```
This class provides a static method `generateRandomString` that generates a random string of a specified length using the given character set. The character set supports both uppercase and lowercase letters, digits, and special characters. The method uses the `rand` function to generate a random index within the character set, and then appends the corresponding character to the resulting string. The method returns the generated random string.

You can use this class to generate random strings in your PHP code by calling its `generateRandomString` method with the desired length as an argument. For example:
```
$randomString = SecurePasswordManager::generateRandomString(10);
echo $randomString;
```
