The `clearCache()` method clears the cache, allowing the parser to free up memory. The `parseJSON(String json)` method parses a given JSON string and returns the root node as an `ObjectNode`. The `getObject(JsonNode json, String path)` method extracts an object node from the JSON document at the specified path, returning it as an `ObjectNode`. The `getList(JsonNode json, String path)` method extracts a list of object nodes from the JSON document at the specified path, returning them as a list of `ObjectNode` objects. The `getString(JsonNode json, String path)` method extracts a string value from the JSON document at the specified path, returning it as a `String`. The `getInt(JsonNode json, String path)` method extracts an integer value from the JSON document at the specified path, returning it as an `int`. The `getLong(JsonNode json, String path)` method extracts a long value from the JSON document at the specified path, returning it as a `long`. The `getBoolean(JsonNode json, String path)` method extracts a boolean value from the JSON document at the specified path, returning it as a `boolean`.

The `validateJSON(String json, JSONObject schema)` method validates a given JSON string against a given JSON schema, throwing an exception if the validation fails. The `rateLimitAPICall(String url)` and `retryAPICall(String url, int numRetries)` methods implement API call rate limiting and retry mechanisms as needed.

