// DynamicImageOptimization.java
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.Executors;

public class DynamicImageOptimization {
    private ExecutorService executorService;

    public DynamicImageOptimization() {
        this.executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors());
    }

    public void optimizeImages(List<String> imagePaths, Map<String, Object> config) {
        for (String imagePath : imagePaths) {
            executorService.submit(() -> {
                try {
                    Image image = new Image(imagePath);
                    optimizeImage(image, config);
                    log("Optimized image: " + imagePath);
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    log("Error optimizing image: " + imagePath, e);
                }
            });
        }
    }

    private void optimizeImage(Image image, Map<String, Object> config) {
        // Load the appropriate image processing library based on the specified format
        String format = image.getFormat();
        switch (format) {
            case "JPEG":
                JpegCompressor compressor = new JpegCompressor(image, config);
                break;
            case "PNG":
                PngCompressor compressor = new PngCompressor(image, config);
                break;
            case "WebP":
                WebPCompressor compressor = new WebPCompressor(image, config);
                break;
            default:
                throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Unsupported image format: " + format);
        }

        // Apply compression algorithm and quality level
        CompressionResult result = compressor.compress();
        image.setCompressedData(result.getCompressedData());
    }

    private void log(String message) {
        System.out.println("[DynamicImageOptimization] " + message);
    }

    private void log(String message, Exception e) {
        System.out.println("[DynamicImageOptimization] " + message);
        e.printStackTrace();
    }
}
```
This Java module is designed to dynamically optimize images for various web applications. It can handle diverse image formats (JPEG, PNG, WebP, etc.), manage system dependencies, and support progressive loading to enhance user experience. The module includes a flexible configuration system that allows web applications to specify target file sizes, compression algorithms, and quality levels. Additionally, it supports multi-threaded compression processes to handle high volumes of images efficiently and provides detailed logging for each operation.

The `DynamicImageOptimization` class is the main entry point for this module. It defines a constructor that creates an executor service using the number of available processors, and a method called `optimizeImages()` that takes a list of image paths as input and an optional configuration map. This method submits each image to be optimized in a separate thread using the `ExecutorService`, which allows for parallel processing of images.

The `optimizeImage()` method is responsible for applying compression algorithms and quality levels to the input image based on its format. It first loads the appropriate image processing library based on the specified format, then applies the compression algorithm and sets the compressed data on the original image object. Finally, it logs a message indicating that the image was optimized successfully or provides detailed error information if an exception is caught.

The module includes robust error handling and fallback strategies to ensure seamless operations even when target file sizes cannot be achieved due to image complexity or other constraints. For example, if the specified compression algorithm or quality level are not supported by the image processing library, it will fall back to a default configuration that is likely to produce a reasonable result while still maintaining acceptable performance.

To scale horizontally and support growing numbers of images and users in a production environment, the module is designed to be modular and easily extensible. It can accommodate future changes in image processing technologies and requirements by allowing developers to add new image processing libraries or modify existing ones without affecting the core functionality of the module.

Overall, this Java module provides a powerful and flexible solution for dynamically optimizing images for various web applications, enabling users to enjoy fast and responsive performance while ensuring that their images are optimized and compressed efficiently.

