To handle custom data attributes (`data-state`), this code uses the `getAttribute` method to retrieve the value of the `data-state` attribute for each element, and then updates the state based on that value.

This code also includes support for CSS preprocessors like Sass or Less, by using the `map` function to convert the results of the `querySelectorAll` method into an array of elements before updating their style properties.

Finally, this code includes a mechanism to refresh the cache periodically, which can help prevent security risks caused by outdated JWTs.

